<% content_for :title, "Help — Caselight" %>
<div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6 py-8">
  <h1 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900">Help</h1>

  <section class="card mt-6 p-5">
    <h2 class="text-sm font-bold text-gray-900">Search syntax</h2>
    <dl class="mt-3 space-y-2 text-sm">
      <% {
        "Natural language" => "Just ask: “when can a court disregard the corporate entity?” — hybrid keyword + semantic search.",
        "Citation" => "Paste “987 F.3d 1234” or “28 U.S.C. § 1331” for a direct fetch.",
        "AND / OR / NOT (%)" => "fraud AND undercapitalization NOT contract",
        "\"phrase\"" => "\"alter ego\" — exact phrase",
        "/n  /s  /p" => "veil /5 pierc! — within 5 words; /s same sentence; /p same paragraph",
        "! and *" => "litigat! expands the root; wom*n matches wildcards",
        "( )" => "fraud AND (alter! OR instrumentality) — grouping"
      }.each do |term, explanation| %>
        <div class="grid grid-cols-[10rem_1fr] gap-3">
          <dt class="font-mono text-xs font-semibold text-brand-800"><%= term %></dt>
          <dd class="text-gray-600"><%= explanation %></dd>
        </div>
      <% end %>
    </dl>
  </section>

  <section class="card mt-5 p-5">
    <h2 class="text-sm font-bold text-gray-900">Treatment flags</h2>
    <ul class="mt-3 space-y-2 text-sm text-gray-600">
      <li><span class="badge-green">Good Law</span> — followed, affirmed, or cited without negative treatment.</li>
      <li><span class="badge-yellow">Caution</span> — distinguished, limited, criticized, questioned, or doubted by some courts.</li>
      <li><span class="badge-red">Negative</span> — overruled, reversed, vacated, abrogated, or superseded. Do not rely without checking.</li>
      <li><span class="badge-gray">Unreviewed</span> — no inbound citations analyzed yet.</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="mt-3 text-xs text-gray-500">The flag is the worst signal across all citing references and is recomputed automatically as new documents ingest.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="card mt-5 p-5">
    <h2 class="text-sm font-bold text-gray-900">Brief checking</h2>
    <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-gray-600">
      Upload a brief under <%= link_to "Documents", uploads_path, class: "font-medium text-brand-700 hover:underline" %>.
      Text is extracted (MinerU/pdftotext/OCR fallbacks), every citation — including short forms,
      <em>id.</em>, and <em>supra</em> — is parsed with eyecite and matched to the corpus, and each authority
      gets a clean / cautionary / negative status. Export the table of authorities as CSV or DOCX.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="card mt-5 p-5">
    <h2 class="text-sm font-bold text-gray-900">About</h2>
    <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-gray-600">
      Caselight is an open-source legal research platform. Corpus data can be imported from public sources
      (CourtListener / RECAP bulk data and API). AI answers are grounded in retrieved passages and always cite their sources.
      Nothing here is legal advice.
    </p>
  </section>
</div>
